[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two matte ceramic plates set at a 3/4 overhead angle of 40 degrees, centered to ensure all contents are visible. Each plate holds three distinct, irregularly shaped dark chocolate and apricot clusters. The clusters have a deep, rich matte brown color from the 70% dark chocolate, with vibrant golden-orange bits of finely chopped dried apricot and tan pieces of roasted almond protruding from the hardened chocolate surface. Dark green pumpkin seeds are visible embedded within the chocolate, and each cluster is topped with a light dusting of coarse, translucent flakes of sea salt that catch the light. The depth of field is shallow, with the nearest plate perfectly sharp and the second plate slightly blurred in the background. Lighting is soft, natural side light from a window on the left, casting gentle, natural shadows. The plates rest on a rustic, aged oak wood table with visible grain and natural wear. Props include a small, rumpled linen napkin pushed to the side, a few loose, chopped almond fragments and a single stray pumpkin seed scattered naturally near the plate rim. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Not a sterile studio setup. Includes slight natural imperfections: a tiny smudge of chocolate on the plate, uneven cluster shapes, and scattered ingredients. Warm, golden-hour color temperature, cozy and inviting. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
  }
]
